# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# The Formspree form id, from https://formspree.io — the part after /f/ in the
# endpoint URL. Eight lowercase letters, e.g. PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ID=abcdefgh
#
# THE BUILD FAILS IF THIS IS MISSING OR EMPTY, deliberately. `astro.config.mjs`
# declares it in `env.schema` as a required field, and Astro coerces an empty
# string to missing before validating. Without that guard a deploy host with no
# environment variable set would emit a form posting to nowhere and still pass
# `npm run verify` — a working-looking contact page that silently drops every
# enquiry. See `src/config/formspree.ts`.
#
# The value is not a secret: it is public by design and appears in the `action`
# attribute of every built contact page. It lives in an env var so the endpoint
# can differ per environment and so the guard above has something to check, not
# to keep it hidden.
PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ID=
